abstract: >
  An open-source digital reference for the Banu Shahr (Shahran; بنو شهر, شَهْران)
  tribe of the Asir and Al-Bahah regions in southwestern Saudi Arabia — its
  history, lineage, sub-branches (Banu Fahm, Banu Nahd, Banu Fayez, Banu Talhah,
  Banu Hassan), notable figures, regional geography, and the cultural traditions
  of poetry, dance, and craft that define the tribe.
